Theorem CN-Ordering: CN-8 fires before CN-6 (commutativity check)

  Preconditions:
    - Input: (Borrowed, HeapEscaping, Unique)
    - CN-8 and CN-6 are both active canonicalization rules
    - Annex E §AIMS + compiler at ori_arc/src/aims/lattice/mod.rs:
      298-300 documents the ordering rationale

  Soundness property:
    CN-8-then-CN-6 =/= CN-6-then-CN-8 on (Borrowed, HeapEscaping, Unique).
    The correct ordering (CN-8 first) preserves Uniqueness=Unique; the
    wrong ordering demotes to MaybeShared.

  Proof obligation:
    CN-8-then-CN-6 path:
      CN-8 fires: Locality HeapEscaping to FunctionLocal (Borrowed + wide).
      State: (Borrowed, FunctionLocal, Unique).
      CN-6 does NOT fire: FunctionLocal < HeapEscaping.
      Final: (Borrowed, FunctionLocal, Unique).

    CN-6-then-CN-8 path:
      CN-6 fires: Uniqueness Unique to MaybeShared (Locality >= HeapEscaping).
      State: (Borrowed, HeapEscaping, MaybeShared).
      CN-8 fires: Locality HeapEscaping to FunctionLocal.
      Final: (Borrowed, FunctionLocal, MaybeShared).

    Outcomes differ on Uniqueness; confirms ordering is load-bearing.

    Engines dispatched:
      case_analysis (commutativity-divergence check per
        section_03::verify_cn_rule_ordering_cn8_before_cn6)

  Expected:
    status: valid
    reason: section_03 case_analysis engine discharges CN-Ordering via two-path commutativity-divergence check
